window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p><b>In the wake of the zombie apocalypse, I thought things couldn't get any worse. I was wrong.</b></p> <p>Struggling to survive in a world turned upside down, I'm haunted by the loss of my parents and the recent disappearance of my twin, Holden. I can't shake the feeling that everything is on the brink of falling apart again. Just when I'm about to lose hope, three strangers arrive at Rolling Hills, seeking help and refuge.</p> <p>Adrian, Theo, and Kenji bring more than just survival skills—they bring a glimmer of hope and a sense of normalcy I haven't felt in a long time. They integrate themselves into my life and the lives of those around me, becoming indispensable to our community. Their presence is both comforting and unsettling, as I grapple with the fear of letting anyone get too close.</p> <p>Can I trust these newcomers? Can I let down my guard and open my heart, or will the secrets I hold bring everything crashing down once more?</p> <p>In a world where trust is a luxury and betrayal can be fatal, I must navigate the fine line between hope and heartbreak. Will I find the strength to let them in, or will my past fears keep me locked away forever?</p> <p><i>This is part one of a two-part duet and is a why-choose-romance, meaning the heroine will not have to choose between the three heroes.</i></p> <p><i>Contains mature content. A complete list of content warnings can be found on the author's website.</i></p>"; 
